course: dictionary
lesson: 3371
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around them tells you which one to use. In «the King keeps threatening to have him executed», the clues are threatening and punishment. So execute here means to put someone to death as a punishment, ordered by a ruler or a court.
explain: Execute can also mean to carry out a plan, an order or a task. «Execute a plan» means do it exactly as it was decided. In sport and dance it means to perform a movement well, as in «execute a perfect cartwheel».
explain: On a computer, to execute a program means to run it. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «The computer executes the code» still makes sense as «the computer runs the code», so you have chosen the right meaning.
explain: The Gryphon says «they never executes nobody», which is country talk. In standard English we say «they never execute anybody». The verb changes its ending: execute, executes, executed, executing.
fact: Execute is a verb. Its forms are execute, executes, executed and executing.
fact: «Execute» can mean to carry out a plan, an order or a task.
fact: «Execute» can mean to perform a movement or skill well, such as a dance step or a dive.
fact: «Execute» can mean to put someone to death as a punishment ordered by a court or ruler, as in kings and traitors long ago.
fact: «Execute» can also mean to run a program or a command on a computer.
exercise: «The gymnast wanted to execute a perfect cartwheel.» What does execute mean here? | Forget it | Put to death | *Do it exactly and well | Write it down
exercise: «The computer will execute the program when you press Enter.» What does execute mean here? | Delete | Sleep through | *Run | Paint
exercise: «The officer executed the order at dawn.» Find and copy the form of execute used in this sentence. | execute | *executed | executes | executing
test: «The team will execute their plan tomorrow.» What does execute mean here? | Argue about | Stop | *Carry out | Give up
test: The Gryphon says «they never executes nobody». Which is the standard English version? | they execute nobody never | *they never execute anybody | they never executed anybody | they never executes nobody
exam: In «She'll get me executed, as sure as ferrets are ferrets!», executed means | Given a prize | Rescued from danger | *Put to death as a punishment | Hidden in a flower-pot
